## 2. Common Instructions
*Syntax: `opcode dest, src1, src2`*

### Arithmetic & Logic
* `add rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 + rs2`
* `addi rd, rs1, imm`  - `rd = rs1 + imm` (Add Immediate)
* `sub rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 - rs2`
* `and rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 & rs2` (Bitwise AND)
* `or rd, rs1, rs2`    - `rd = rs1 | rs2` (Bitwise OR)
* `xor rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 ^ rs2` (Bitwise XOR)

### Shifts
* `sll rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 << rs2` (Shift Left Logical)
* `srl rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 >> rs2` (Shift Right Logical)
* `sra rd, rs1, rs2`   - `rd = rs1 >> rs2` (Shift Right Arithmetic, preserves sign bit)

### Memory Operations (Load & Store)
*Note: Memory addresses are formed by adding an offset immediate to a base register: `offset(register)`*
* `lw rd, offset(rs1)`  - Load 32-bit Word from memory into `rd`
* `lh rd, offset(rs1)`  - Load 16-bit Halfword (sign-extended) into `rd`
* `lb rd, offset(rs1)`  - Load 8-bit Byte (sign-extended) into `rd`
* `sw rs2, offset(rs1)` - Store 32-bit Word from `rs2` into memory
* `sh rs2, offset(rs1)` - Store 16-bit Halfword from `rs2` into memory
* `sb rs2, offset(rs1)` - Store 8-bit Byte from `rs2` into memory

### Conditional Branches
*Syntax: `op rs1, rs2, label`*
* `beq rs1, rs2, label`  - Branch to `label` if `rs1 == rs2`
* `bne rs1, rs2, label`  - Branch to `label` if `rs1 != rs2`
* `blt rs1, rs2, label`  - Branch to `label` if `rs1 < rs2` (signed)
* `bge rs1, rs2, label`  - Branch to `label` if `rs1 >= rs2` (signed)

### Unconditional Jumps
* `jal rd, label`        - Jump to `label` and store return address PC+4 in `rd` (usually `ra`)
* `jalr rd, offset(rs1)` - Jump to `rs1 + offset` and store return address PC+4 in `rd`

