## 3. Common Pseudo-Instructions
Shorthand codes written by programmers that the assembler maps to core hardware instructions.

* `li rd, imm`      - Load Immediate (Maps to: `addi rd, zero, imm`)
* `mv rd, rs`       - Copy Register (Maps to: `addi rd, rs, 0`)
* `j label`         - Unconditional Jump (Maps to: `jal zero, label`)
* `jr rs`           - Jump Register (Maps to: `jalr zero, 0(rs)`)
* `ret`             - Return from subroutine (Maps to: `jalr zero, 0(ra)`)
* `nop`             - No Operation (Maps to: `addi zero, zero, 0`)

